WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:04.340
Body and stunt doubles are the unsung heroes
of the movie industry, putting themselves

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:07.750
on the line so actors getting paid a lot more
money get to look awesome.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.080
Thanks to the magic of editing, stunt doubles
don't have to look all that much like the

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.240
actor they're filling in for, but sometimes
a production needs someone with a strong physical

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.520
resemblance to a star.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.190
Who better to call on than an actor's close
relative?

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.619
These films took advantage of shared DNA to
pull off some tricky scenes, leaving audiences

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:24.830
none the wiser.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.310
Pirates of the Caribbean: On Stranger Tides

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:31.210
In the fourth installment of the Pirates of
the Caribbean franchise, series leading lady

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.320
Keira Knightley was replaced by Penélope
Cruz, who got some great news soon after the

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.030
filming of On Stranger Tides began ...

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.210
"I am with child.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.030
Yours!"

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.870
The father is actually fellow Spanish actor
Javier Bardem, the villain of the film's follow-up,

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.280
Dead Men Tell No Tales.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.670
The news put a kink in the production's plans,
considering her character is introduced in

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.850
a tricky three-minute swordfighting scene
her doctor would likely deem too risky.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.680
Sure, she's dressed up like Jack Sparrow …

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:00.879
"Hello Angelica."

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:04.089
"Hello Jack."

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:07.779
… so they could have used any ol' stunt
double, but Cruz's younger sister Monica proved

00:01:07.779 --> 00:01:11.560
to be a far better match, as a trained dancer
with swordfighting experience.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.060
Monica reportedly doubled for Penélope during
most of her fight scenes, as well as a number

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:20.020
of full body shots later in production to
hide her sister's burgeoning baby bump.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.020
Forrest Gump

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.790
Tom Hanks didn't actually pound the pavement
the entire time they were filming those cross-country

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.259
running scenes in Forrest Gump.

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:29.979
His younger brother Jim filled in for him
for a few hundred yards shot in Montana and

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:30.979
South Carolina.

00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:35.659
Along with bearing a strong physical resemblance
to his brother, Jim's voice is virtually identical

00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:36.659
to that of his famous sibling …

00:01:36.659 --> 00:01:39.469
"There's no crying in voicemail!"

00:01:39.469 --> 00:01:43.919
… which has earned him gigs voicing Sheriff
Woody in Toy Story video games, straight-to-DVD

00:01:43.919 --> 00:01:44.919
movies, and more …

00:01:44.919 --> 00:01:45.919
"Ha ha!

00:01:45.919 --> 00:01:47.299
Boy am I glad to see you."

00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:48.299
"Is that you?"

00:01:48.299 --> 00:01:50.359
"No, it's my brother, Jim."

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:51.359
(Laughter)

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.060
"Is that really?"

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.060
"Yeah."

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.520
Furious 7

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:58.999
After Paul Walker's untimely death in 2013
midway through filming Furious 7, the future

00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:02.349
of the entire Fast and the Furious franchise
was called into question.

00:02:02.349 --> 00:02:05.639
Production was temporarily halted while the
studio sorted out options—one of which was

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:09.640
using CGI to put his face onto one of his
two brothers, Caleb and Cody, and have them

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.209
film the rest of his scenes.

00:02:11.209 --> 00:02:15.700
With the exception of a few CGI shots deconstructed
to show the process used to revive him for

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.750
the role, the studio hasn't revealed which
scenes are real and which are fake, but about

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:22.080
350 overall shots had to be altered.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.709
The end result is a film where it's near impossible
to tell exactly when you're looking at Paul

00:02:25.709 --> 00:02:30.709
Walker, re-purposed footage spliced into the
scene, his face CGI'd onto one of his brother's

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:33.489
bodies, or even a combination of all three.

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:34.849
Most of The Rock's movies

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:38.650
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson is a physically
massive human being, so there aren't too many

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.569
stuntmen who could convincingly pretend to
be him, right?

00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:46.280
Well, there is one: Tanoai Reed, who also
happens to be his cousin … and also happens

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.280
to be the size of a refrigerator.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.840
"This has nothing to do with saving people.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.280
These are refrigerators."

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.120
"This is Baywatch, p----!"

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.020
As one of the few human beings with arms equal
in size to his cousin, Reed has been working

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.769
as his stunt double for virtually his entire
acting career.

00:02:59.769 --> 00:03:03.730
In fact, Reed has doubled for his cousin for
so long, he appeared in the films that still

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:07.739
credited Dwayne as "The Rock", the ones in
which he starred as Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson,

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:12.829
and, of course, the more recent blockbusters
crediting him simply as Dwayne Johnson, including

00:03:12.829 --> 00:03:13.829
the Baywatch reboot …

00:03:13.829 --> 00:03:15.500
"If you want me, you can have me."

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.680
"Some other time."

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.019
Thanks for watching!

